# Read the gold a Craft repair asks for, against the item's own hit points and
# base value (bd inc-nc1). tools/check_repair_cost.sh reads the three dumps.
#
# WHY THIS FIXTURE. human-paladin-seed4-opt0822.sav wears leather armour +3, a
# 2136 gp item that is not metal, so Craft needs no forge. It carries 11 gp, so
# the repair stops at "That would cost N gp in materials, but you only have 11
# gp." -- the same gpCost the Proceed prompt prints, with nothing spent.
#
# HOW THE ARMOUR GETS DAMAGED. A wizard-made "minor decay trap" is placed on the
# square to the east and walked onto. At seed 1 the trap hits the armour and
# leaves it at 78/86 hit points. The first RIGHT after the placement is eaten by
# the "You find a trap" interrupt; the second RIGHT opens the confirm prompt.
#
# WHAT IS DUMPED. exam: the item's description ("base value of N gp", "N out of
# M hit points"). menu: the "Repair which item?" list with (hp/max). cost: the
# gold message.

w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Create Trap"
"minor decay trap" ENTER
RIGHT
ENTER
RIGHT
RIGHT
y

i
j
x
@dump:exam
ESC
ESC

u
@choose "Craft"
r
@dump:menu
a
@dump:cost
